window.NPC_CHUNK_243 = [{"name":"Red Mantis Assassin","cr":8,"xp":4800,"race":"human","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"fighter","level":3},{"class":"red mantis assassin","level":3},{"class":"rogue","level":3}],"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":4,"ac":19,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+3 armor, +4 Dex, +1 dodge, +1 shield","hp":78,"hd":"6d8+3d10+30","hd_value":9,"fort":8,"ref":11,"will":5,"save_mods":"Will: +1 vs. fear","defensive_abilities":["evasion","red shroud (2/day, 3 rounds)","trap sense +1"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"+1 sawtooth sabre +11 (1d8+8/19-20), +1 sawtooth sabre +11 (1d8+6/19-20)","ranged":"dagger +11 (1d4+5/19-20)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"prayer attack","details":"DC 16"},{"type":"sneak attack","details":"+3d6"}],"spellsknown_caster":"red mantis assassin","spellsknown_caster_level":3,"spellsknown_concentration":4,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"expeditious retreat"},{"spell":"feather fall"},{"spell":"magic weapon"},{"spell":"vanish"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":18,"constitution":14,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":10,"charisma":12,"baseatk":7,"cmb":11,"cmd":26,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Arcane Strike"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Exotic Weapon Proficiency (sawtooth sabre)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Two-Weapon Defense"},{"feat":"Two-Weapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (sawtooth sabre)"},{"feat":"Weapon Specialization (sawtooth sabre)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":16},{"skill":"Bluff","value":10},{"skill":"Climb","value":16},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":2},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16}],"languages":["Common"],"sq":["armor training 1","rogue talent (finesse rogue)","trapfinding +1"],"special_abilities":[{"type":"Prayer Attack","kind":"Su","details":"To initiate a prayer attack, a Red Mantis assassin holds her sawtooth sabre (or sabres) out, point down, and weaves the blade in the air. She must be within 30 ft. of and visible to her victim. Beginning a prayer attack is a standard action, and causes her victim to be fascinated by her unless he succeeds at a DC 16 Will save. She can maintain the fascination effect by concentrating. The victim can attempt a new save to escape fascination each time a threat (other than the assassin) appears. At any point after 3 rounds, the assassin can make a coup de grace attack against the target, provided the target is still fascinated. Activating or concentrating on maintaining a prayer attack doesn't provoke an attack of opportunity."},{"type":"Red Shroud","kind":"Su","details":"A Red Mantis assassin can create a veil of red mist two times per day as a move action. The red shroud persists for 3 rounds. It grants a +1 dodge bonus to Armor Class and fast healing 2. This mist cannot be dissipated by wind. If she is slain while this ability is active, she can choose whether to remain corporeal or to disintegrate into a cloud of red mist that leaves behind only her gear in order to deprive her enemies of access to her remains."}],"gear":"+1 leather armor, +1 sawtooth sabres (2), daggers (4), cloak of resistance +1, mask of the mantis, 27 pp, potion of bull's strength (2), potion of resist fire, alchemist's fire (2)","before_combat":"As soon as the assassins realize someone's entering the house, they each drink a potion of resist fire and a potion of bull's strength, cast magic weapon on their blades, and spend charges from their masks to activate all of the masks' abilities (using the effects of deathwatch at day or darkvision at night). They then remain hidden until they are spotted or until at least one PC climbs the stairs up to area A7.","during_combat":"The assassins are outnumbered, but they've got a deadly advantage: just as in their previous attempt to slay Vencarlo, they crept into the ambush site early and prepared the place with distilled alchemist's fire. On the first round of combat, each assassin throws a vial of alchemist's fire at the fireplace on her level, causing flames to burst out and quickly light the room on fire. The 3 squares the fireplace takes up are now burning-each round, the fire spreads quickly to 1d4 adjacent squares. A character in a square that is on fire takes 1d6 points of fire damage and must succeed at a DC 15 Reflex save or catch on fire. The Red Mantis assassins need not fear the fire as long as their potions last, and they use the fire to their advantage as they are able. Once the battle begins, the assassins each activate their red shroud ability and make an effort to reach each other so they can team up and flank foes. If the assassins begin combat with only one PC in sight, an assassin attempts to use his prayer attack on that PC before starting his fire.","morale":"The assassins fight to the death.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3, Pathfinder RPG Campaign Setting: The Inner Sea World Guide 282"},{"name":"Pilts Swastel","cr":10,"xp":9600,"race":"human","gender":"Male","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"bard","level":11}],"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":4,"ac":22,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+5 armor, +3 Dex, +4 natural","hp":97,"hd":"11d8+44","hd_value":11,"fort":7,"ref":13,"will":8,"save_mods":"+4 vs. bardic performance, language-dependent, and sonic","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"mwk war razor +13 (1d4/19-20)","ranged":"mwk light crossbow +13 (1d8/19-20)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"bardic performance 28 rounds/day","details":"move action; countersong, dirge of doom, distraction, fascinate [DC 19], inspire competence +4, inspire courage +3, inspire greatness, suggestion [DC 19]"}],"spellsknown_caster":"bard","spellsknown_caster_level":11,"spellsknown_concentration":15,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":3,"spells":[{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"modify memory"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"confusion"},{"spell":"displacement"},{"spell":"glibness"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"cat's grace"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"hold person"},{"spell":"mirror image"},{"spell":"tongues"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"cure light wounds"},{"spell":"grease"},{"spell":"undetectable alignment"},{"spell":"unseen servant"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"open/close"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"}]}],"strength":10,"dexterity":18,"constitution":14,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":8,"charisma":19,"baseatk":8,"cmb":8,"cmd":22,"feats":[{"feat":"Craft Rod"},{"feat":"Craft Wondrous Item"},{"feat":"Leadership"},{"feat":"Martial Weapon Proficiency (war razor)"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Perform (act)","value":18},{"skill":"Perform (comedy)","value":18},{"skill":"Perform (oratory)","value":18},{"skill":"Sleight of Hand","value":15},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15},{"skill":"Survival","value":10}],"languages":["Common","Gnome","Varisian"],"sq":["bardic knowledge +5","jack-of-all-trades","lore master 2/day","versatile performances (act, comedy, oratory)"],"gear":"+1 glamered chain shirt, mwk light crossbow with 10 bolts, mwk war razor, cloak of resistance +2, headband of alluring charisma +2, 291 gp, potion of barkskin +4 (2), rod of wonder","before_combat":"Pilts casts alarm on the door to Salvator's cell every morning, and unseen servant and undetectable alignment as soon as he takes his throne for the day. As soon as he realizes he's about to have visitors, he also casts glibness and tongues on himself. Before Pilts enters combat, he makes sure to drink his potion of barkskin +4 and casts cat's grace.","during_combat":"Pilts orders his minions to the attack, supporting them with inspire courage on the first round of combat. He then alternates casting spells such as confusion, charm monster, and hold person with activations of his rod of wonder. Each time he successfully uses this unpredictable device, he shrieks in delight and offers impromptu commentary on the rod's results. As soon as it seems obvious that he's about to be attacked, he casts displacement on himself and fights back with his war razor.","morale":"If brought below 20 hit points, the emperor uses dimension door to go to his bedroom (area C11), then takes 3d6 rounds gathering up his favorite prizes before using dimension door again (or by fleeing via area C7) to hide out in Old Dock and nurse his wounds and plan his revenge against the PCs. If he's brought below 10 hit points and unable to use dimension door, Pilts's bravado crumbles. He drops to his knees and begs pitifully for his life, offering up pretty much anything to the PCs in return for mercy. In either event, as soon as Pilts is killed or surrenders publicly (or 2d6 rounds after he flees), his mob falls to pieces and the thugs scatter, seeking a safe place to recover and figure out what to do next.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3"},{"name":"Jabbyr","cr":8,"xp":4800,"race":"gnome","gender":"Male","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"barbarian","level":9}],"alignment":"CE","size":"Small","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["gnome"],"init":6,"senses":["low-light vision"],"ac":16,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+3 armor, +2 Dex, +1 dodge, +1 natural, -2 rage, +1 size","hp":118,"hd":"9d12+54","hd_value":9,"fort":11,"ref":5,"will":8,"save_mods":"+2 vs. illusions","defensive_abilities":["defensive training","improved uncanny dodge","trap sense +3"],"dr":"1/-","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":35}],"melee":"+1 greataxe +17 (1d10+8/x3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"hatred"},{"type":"rage","details":"23 rounds/day"},{"type":"rage powers","details":"clear mind, guarded stance +2, no escape, swift foot"}],"strength":20,"dexterity":14,"constitution":20,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":12,"charisma":5,"baseatk":9,"cmb":13,"cmd":24,"feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (greataxe)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":15}],"languages":["Common","Gnome","Sylvan"],"sq":["fast movement","gnome magic"],"gear":"+1 leather armor, +1 greataxe, amulet of natural armor +1, belt of giant strength +2","before_combat":"As soon as combat begins, Jabbyr rages.","during_combat":"Jabbyr follows Pilts's commands exactly, attacking whomever the emperor orders him to. Left to his own devices, Jabbyr tends to focus on whatever enemy is closest. The single exception to this is gnomes, as Jabbyr attacks other gnomes only in response to being attacked by one of them first. Pilts knows better than to order the insane barbarian to attack another gnome, in any event.","morale":"Jabbyr fights to the death. If he discovers that Pilts has been killed, he freezes in shock for 1 round before continuing his rage (this round of no actions still depletes his available rounds of raging as normal). On the other hand, if Pilts surrenders in Jabbyr's presence, something inside the gnome snaps and he focuses his wrath on the ex-emperor. Surrendering is tantamount to treason in Jabbyr's mind, and he'd rather have his master slain at his own hands than live with the ignominy of such a defeat. He might even demand that the PCs help him put Pilts into the Tall Knife, although whether the PCs can understand the demented little gnome's tongueless babbling is left for you to determine (at your discretion, this may require a successful DC 20 Sense Motive check).","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3"},{"name":"Choker Brute","cr":3,"xp":800,"race":"Choker","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"rogue","level":1}],"alignment":"CE","size":"Small","type":"aberration","init":6,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft."],"ac":17,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +4 natural, +1 size","hp":34,"hd":"4d8+17","hd_value":4,"fort":5,"ref":5,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"climb","speed":10},{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"2 tentacles +8 (1d4+5 plus grab)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d4+5"},{"type":"grab","details":"Medium"},{"type":"sneak attack","details":"+1d6"},{"type":"strangle"}],"strength":20,"dexterity":14,"constitution":18,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":16,"charisma":5,"baseatk":2,"cmb":6,"cmb_special":"+10 grapple","cmd":18,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":8},{"skill":"Climb","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":10},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15}],"languages":["Undercommon"],"sq":["quickness","trapfinding +1"],"during_combat":"The choker brutes lurk in the shadows in the rafters up above, watching observantly if they notice anyone attempting to move through the room. They swiftly move to attack as soon as they notice anyone outside trying to open the door, or 3 rounds after intruders from the south have already opened the door and are moving about inside the room.","morale":"The choker brutes fight to the death.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 45"},{"name":"Salvator Scream","cr":4,"xp":1200,"race":"human","gender":"Male","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"expert","level":6}],"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":1,"ac":11,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":10,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex","hp":39,"hd":"6d8+12","hd_value":6,"fort":5,"ref":3,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"unarmed strike +4 (1d3 nonlethal)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":10,"dexterity":13,"constitution":12,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":8,"charisma":9,"baseatk":4,"cmb":4,"cmd":15,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Craft)","type":"painting"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":11},{"skill":"Bluff","value":8},{"skill":"Craft (painting)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":11},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":11},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":10},{"skill":"Profession (artist)","value":8},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":10}],"languages":["Common","Aklo","Draconic"],"gear":"painter's equipment, stained clothes","during_combat":"Salvator is no fighter, and he knows it. In combat, he cowers behind his allies, throwing punches only when there's no other choice.","morale":"Salvator flees if all his allies are defeated, or if reduced to fewer than 25 hit points. If he does so, his  primary goal is to find a small dark place to hide, and he eventually works his way back to his home (only to be eaten by the otyughs if the PCs haven't defeated them).","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3"},{"name":"Garden Guardian","cr":7,"xp":3200,"race":"janni genie","age_category":"Adult","alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"plant","sub_types":["native","outsider"],"templates_applied":"fungal","init":5,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft.","low-light vision"],"ac":23,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+7 armor, +1 Dex, +1 dodge, +3 natural, +1 shield","hp":80,"hd":"9d8+27","hd_value":9,"fort":9,"ref":7,"will":5,"defensive_abilities":["poisonous blood"],"immunities":["disease","mind-affecting effects","paralysis","poison","polymorph","sleep","stunning"],"resists":["fire 10"],"weaknesses":["worldbound"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":5,"maneuverability":"perfect"},{"type":"land","speed":20,"special":"30 ft. without armor"}],"melee":"+1 scimitar +16 (1d6+6/15-20)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"poison spore cloud"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":9,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"create food and water"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"change size"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"invisibility","details":"self only"},{"spell":"speak with animals"}]}],"strength":20,"dexterity":13,"constitution":16,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":15,"charisma":13,"baseatk":9,"cmb":14,"cmd":26,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (scimitar)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (scimitar)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":14},{"skill":"Craft (weapons)","value":12},{"skill":"Fly","value":17},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Ride","value":6},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":14},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9}],"languages":["Common","Sylvan","Terran","Vudrani","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":["elemental endurance","fungal metabolism","rejuvenation"],"special_abilities":[{"type":"Worldbound","kind":"Ex","details":"The garden guardians are transformed jann that have been bound to the Material Plane by Vudrani magic. As a result, they don't have the ability to use ethereal jaunt or plane shift as spell-like abilities. Because of their unique nature, they also lack the create spawn ability possessed by most fungal creatures."}],"gear":"+1 chainmail, mwk light steel shield, +1 scimitar","before_combat":"The garden guardians become invisible as soon as they hear anything or anyone approaching the area they protect.","during_combat":"These fungal creatures open combat with their poison spore clouds, following that up with melee attacks. They avoid using their change size ability to increase their own size so as to maintain more mobility on the ledge, but don't hesitate to reduce the size of particularly strong foes.","morale":"The fungal janni fight to the death, pursuing foes throughout the entire cavern (but not into area D24, area D25 or the palace above).","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 4 116, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 141"},{"name":"Enormous Reefclaw","cr":10,"xp":9600,"race":"reefclaw","age_category":"Adult","alignment":"CN","size":"Large","type":"aberration","sub_types":["aquatic"],"init":6,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft.","low-light vision"],"ac":21,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +1 dodge, +9 natural, -1 size","hp":151,"hd":"10d8+70","hd_value":10,"fort":10,"ref":5,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["ferocity"],"resists":["cold 5"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":5},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +14 (1d8+8 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d8+8"},{"type":"death frenzy"},{"type":"grab","details":"any size"},{"type":"poison","details":"DC 22"}],"strength":26,"dexterity":15,"constitution":24,"intelligence":9,"wisdom":16,"charisma":17,"baseatk":7,"cmb":16,"cmb_special":"+24 grapple","cmd":29,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Armor (3)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Swim","value":29}],"languages":["Common (can't speak)"],"sq":["amphibious"],"during_combat":"The reefclaw knows the barge and pier belong to its Arkona allies, and does its best not to damage them. The same gentle touch isn't extended to the PCs, as the monster attacks anyone it regards as an intruder with a ferocious rage.","morale":"The enormous reefclaw gives up the fight if reduced to fewer than 20 hit points, swimming swiftly out to sea to seek new allies. It doesn't return.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 2 234","unique_monster":1},{"name":"Vimanda","cr":12,"xp":19200,"race":"rakshasa","gender":"Female","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"monk","level":5}],"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","sub_types":["native","shapechanger"],"init":9,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft."],"ac":28,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +9 natural, +3 Wis","hp":202,"hd":"5d8+10d10+125","hd_value":15,"fort":15,"ref":16,"will":15,"save_mods":"+2 vs. enchantments","defensive_abilities":["evasion"],"dr":"15/good and piercing","immunities":["disease"],"sr":25,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"+1 ki focus shock kukri +17 (1d4+7/15-20 plus 1d6 electricity) and unarmed strike +11 (1d8+6) or unarmed strike flurry of blows +19 (1d8+6)","ranged":"javelin of lightning +18 (1d6+6)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"detect thoughts"},{"type":"flurry of blows"},{"type":"stunning fist","details":"7/day, DC 19"}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"fly"},{"spell":"suggestion"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"scorching ray"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"expeditious retreat"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"ray of enfeeblement"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"detect poison"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"}]}],"strength":22,"dexterity":20,"constitution":26,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":15,"charisma":20,"baseatk":13,"cmb":21,"cmd":38,"feats":[{"feat":"Arcane Strike"},{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Deflect Arrows"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (kukri)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Unarmed Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Stunning Fist"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (kukri)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":18},{"skill":"Bluff","value":22},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":18},{"skill":"Disguise","value":26},{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Perform (dance)","value":18},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":15},{"skill":"Stealth","value":18}],"languages":["Common","Vudrani"],"sq":["change shape (any humanoid; alter self)","fast movement","high jump","ki pool (4 points, magic)","maneuver training","slow fall 20 ft."],"gear":"+1 ki focus shock kukri, javelins of lightning (2), gold armbands worth 1,400 gp, wand of dimension door (3 charges)","during_combat":"If the PCs see through Vimanda's deception, she snarls and attacks. In combat, she takes to the air and hurls her javelins, as well as casts scorching ray and magic missile. If pushed into melee, she switches to physical attacks, delivering stunning fists with her kukri on her first attack each round. She doesn't assume her true form in battle.","morale":"If Vimanda is brought to fewer than 50 hit points, she attempts to bargain with the PCs, congratulating them on their skill and asking them if they would like her aid in defeating the man who is their true enemy- Bahor. If the PCs don't agree, she uses a precious charge of her wand of dimension door to flee to Old Korvosa and recover from the fight. In time, she could seek out the PCs again for revenge.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 231"},{"name":"Sivit","cr":10,"xp":9600,"race":"darksphinx","gender":"Female","age_category":"Adult","alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"outsider","sub_types":["evil","extraplanar"],"init":3,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft.","detect magic","read magic","see invisibility"],"ac":24,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+3 armor, +3 Dex, +8 natural, +1 shield, -1 size","hp":126,"hd":"11d10+66","hd_value":11,"fort":13,"ref":6,"will":11,"dr":"10/good","immunities":["poison"],"resists":["acid 10","cold 10","electricity 10","fire 10"],"sr":22,"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"+1 kukri +16 (1d6+7/15-20), +1 kukri +16 (1d6+7/15-20), tail slap +11 (1d6+3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"pounce"},{"type":"rake","details":"2 claws +16, 1d6+6"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":15,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"desecrate"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"legend lore"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"remove curse"},{"spell":"unholy blight"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"clairaudience/clairvoyance"},{"spell":"darkness"},{"spell":"poison"}]},{"frequency":"1/week","spells":[{"spell":"symbol of fear"},{"spell":"symbol of pain"},{"spell":"symbol of sleep"},{"spell":"symbol of stunning"}]}],"strength":23,"dexterity":16,"constitution":23,"intelligence":22,"wisdom":19,"charisma":20,"baseatk":11,"cmb":18,"cmd":31,"cmd_special":"35 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Dazzling Display"},{"feat":"Double Slice"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (kukri)"},{"feat":"Two-Weapon Defense"},{"feat":"Two-Weapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (kukri)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":17},{"skill":"Bluff","value":19},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":19},{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Heal","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (engineering)","value":17},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":18},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Survival","value":18},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":16}],"languages":["Common","Celestial","Draconic","Infernal","Sphinx","Vudrani; comprehend languages"],"gear":"+1 leather armor, +1 kukris (2), wand of dimension door (19 charges), wand of magic missile (CL 9th, 18 charges)","before_combat":"Sivit has already used her four symbols, as indicated in the text of the encounters.","during_combat":"Sivit starts combat by casting unholy blight, then moves in to attack foes in melee, to pouncing and raking on the first round of battle. Against ranged foes, she relies on her wand of magic missile.","morale":"Sivit fights to the death, but cannot pursue foes beyond the Vivified Labyrinth's borders.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3, The Book of Fiends 156"},{"name":"Neolandus Kalepopolis","cr":5,"xp":1600,"race":"human","gender":"Male","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"aristocrat","level":3},{"class":"ranger","level":3}],"alignment":"LG","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":7,"ac":13,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":10,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex","hp":34,"hd":"3d8+3d10","hd_value":6,"fort":6,"ref":7,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"unarmed strike +4 (1d3-1 nonlethal)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"combat style (crossbow)"},{"type":"favored enemy","details":"giants +2"}],"strength":8,"dexterity":16,"constitution":10,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":14,"charisma":15,"baseatk":5,"cmb":4,"cmd":17,"feats":[{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Rapid Reload"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Diplomacy)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":11},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":16},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":8},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":4},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":7},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":7},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Ride","value":12},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":11},{"skill":"Survival","value":11}],"languages":["Common","Varisian"],"sq":["favored terrain (mountainous +2)","track +1","wild empathy +5"],"during_combat":"Although Neolandus trained as a ranger, he realizes his true skills are in diplomacy. As such, he only fights when there is no other choice, in which case he prefers to engage in combat with his deity's favored weapon, the light crossbow.","morale":"Neolandus won't abandon an ally, but if alone, flees to safety if brought to fewer than 15 hit points.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3"},{"name":"Rajambari","cr":7,"xp":3200,"race":"mastodon elephant","age_category":"Adult","alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"undead","templates_applied":"@skeleton","init":8,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft."],"ac":17,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +5 natural, -2 size","hp":63,"hd":"14d8","hd_value":14,"fort":4,"ref":8,"will":9,"dr":"5/bludgeoning","immunities":["cold","undead traits"],"weaknesses":["servile"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"gore +22 (2d8+14), slam +22 (2d6+14)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"war stomp"}],"strength":38,"dexterity":18,"wisdom":10,"charisma":10,"baseatk":10,"cmb":26,"cmd":40,"cmd_special":"44 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative","type":"bonus"}],"special_abilities":[{"type":"Servile","kind":"Ex","details":"A rajambari's method of creation makes it far easier to command, and when affected by any spell or effect that allows command over undead creatures, the duration of the effect is doubled. A rajambari can understand the spoken commands of any creature that successfully commands it, regardless of the language."},{"type":"War Stomp","kind":"Su","details":"Upon creation, a rajambari is infused with the ability to perform a war stomp. The mindless undead can perform a war stomp as a standard action once per minute, and they generally do so when first presented with the opportunity against a foe, regardless of whether the tactic is sound or not. When a rajambari war stomps, it slams its front two feet down upon the ground, creating a shock wave that can knock nearby opponents prone. The rajambari attempts a trip combat maneuver against all creatures standing on the ground within a 20-foot radius, including other rajambari."}],"during_combat":"As long as no creatures attempt to damage them or the surrounding structure of the Gizzard, the rajambari remain passive. Once either of  these conditions ends, though, the undead mastodons immediately move to defend the Gizzard. Each mastodon skeleton can move up to 15 ft. from its pillar to attack intruders; as they fight, the chains that attach them to the pillars move and shake, causing the rooms above to shake as well, but as long as the gears remain locked, the rooms above won't shift. If at least two of the skeletal mastodons are destroyed, the remaining ones are not strong enough to rotate the chambers of the Vivified Labyrinth above and the rooms remain stuck in their current configuration.","morale":"The skeletal elephants fight until destroyed.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 3, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 128, 250"},{"name":"Ashwing Gargoyle","cr":5,"xp":1600,"race":"gargoyle","age_category":"Adult","alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"monstrous humanoid","sub_types":["earth"],"templates_applied":"advanced","init":4,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft."],"ac":20,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +6 natural","hp":52,"hd":"5d10+25","hd_value":5,"fort":6,"ref":8,"will":6,"dr":"10/magic","speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"},{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +9 (1d4+4), 2 claws +9 (1d6+4), gore +9 (1d4+4)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":19,"dexterity":18,"constitution":20,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":15,"charisma":11,"baseatk":5,"cmb":9,"cmd":23,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":4},{"skill":"Fly","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":10},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14,"special":"+6 in stony areas"},{"skill":"Survival","value":10}],"languages":["Common","Terran"],"sq":["freeze"],"during_combat":"Ashwing gargoyles hate humans-and among them, hate Shoanti the most. They favor these targets in combat over all others, and often take advantage of Flyby Attack to swoop in and bite at enemies while preventing full attacks in retaliation.","morale":"An Ashwing flees once reduced to fewer than 5 hp.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 288, 137"},{"name":"The Cinderlander","cr":12,"xp":19200,"race":"human","gender":"Male","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"horizon walker","level":3},{"class":"ranger","level":10}],"alignment":"CN","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":4,"ac":25,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+6 armor, +1 deflection, +4 Dex, +1 dodge, +3 natural","hp":151,"hd":"13d10+75","hd_value":13,"fort":13,"ref":12,"will":5,"defensive_abilities":["evasion"],"immunities":["exhaustion","fatigue"],"resists":["fire 10"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"mwk handaxe +15 (1d6+1/x3)","ranged":"Vindicator +15 (1d10+1/17-20)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"combat style (crossbow)"},{"type":"favored enemies","details":"giants +6, humans +2, magical beasts +2"}],"spellsprepared_caster":"ranger","spellsprepared_caster_level":7,"spellsprepared_concentration":8,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"barkskin"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":3,"spells":[{"spell":"charm animal"},{"spell":"gravity bow"},{"spell":"pass without trace"}]}],"strength":12,"dexterity":18,"constitution":18,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":13,"charisma":8,"baseatk":13,"cmb":14,"cmd":30,"feats":[{"feat":"Bleeding Critical"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Deadly Aim"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Exotic Weapon Proficiency (repeating heavy crossbow)"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (repeating heavy crossbow)"},{"feat":"Precise Shot"},{"feat":"Shot On The Run"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (repeating heavy crossbow)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":15},{"skill":"Heal","value":17},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":14},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":5},{"skill":"Perception","value":17},{"skill":"Stealth","value":20},{"skill":"Survival","value":17}],"languages":["Common","Giant","Shoanti"],"sq":["favored terrains (desert +6, mountainous +2, plains +2, urban +2)","hunter's bond (firepelt cougar named Neverfar)","swift tracker","terrain dominance (desert)","terrain mastery (desert)","track +5","wild empathy +9","woodland stride"],"gear":"+2 mithral chain shirt, Vindicator (+1 Human-bane repeating heavy crossbow) with 20 screaming bolts and 10 bolts, mwk handaxe, belt of incredible dexterity +2, ring of protection +1, survival kit, potion of haste, wand of cure moderate wounds (8 charges)","before_combat":"The Cinderlander casts pass without trace before going on any scouting missions. Before engaging in combat, the Cinderlander casts barkskin on himself.","during_combat":"The Cinderlander prefers to fight at range with Vindicator, casting gravity bow on the crossbow and then targeting Shoanti to the exclusion of all other foes if given a choice. A favorite tactic against mounted enemies is to cast charm animal on a mount to lessen its rider's mobility. He resorts to his masterwork handaxe only when forced to. His animal companion Neverfar remains at his side-the Cinderlander prefers to use the firepelt cougar as a guardian while he sleeps rather than as a bodyguard or assassin.","morale":"Although far from cowardly, the Cinderlander doesn't particularly like the Red Mantis. He can be bought, and for a bribe of no less than 500 gp, he abandons Cinnabar and the assassins to their fate, even switching sides in the middle of combat. He's seen what they're capable of, though, and isn't particularly interested in picking a fight against them. In any event, he attempts to flee if brought to fewer than 20 hit points.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4, Pathfinder RPG Advanced Player's Guide 265"},{"name":"Neverfar","xp":0,"race":"firepelt cougar (leopard)","gender":"Male","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"animal companion","level":7}],"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"animal","init":5,"senses":["low-light vision","scent"],"ac":21,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +5 natural","hp":51,"hd":"6d8+24","hd_value":6,"fort":8,"ref":10,"will":3,"save_mods":"Will: +4 morale bonus vs. enchantments","defensive_abilities":["evasion"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +9 (1d6+4), 2 claws +9 (1d3+4)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":18,"dexterity":21,"constitution":16,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":12,"charisma":6,"baseatk":4,"cmb":8,"cmd":24,"cmd_special":"28 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":7},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11,"special":"+4 in undergrowth"}],"sq":["devotion"],"during_combat":"Neverfar has been trained to attack Shoanti in preference to all other targets, but if the Cinderlander is hurt by a foe, the firepelt focuses on that enemy instead.","morale":"Neverfar fights to the death as long as the Cinderlander lives. If the Cinderlander is killed, the cougar defends the man's body to the death.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4"},{"name":"Krojun Eats-What-He-Kills","cr":12,"xp":19200,"race":"human","gender":"Male","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"barbarian","level":13}],"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":2,"senses":["scent"],"ac":22,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+6 armor, +2 deflection, +2 Dex, +1 natural, -2 rage, +3 shield","hp":181,"hd":"13d12+91","hd_value":13,"fort":14,"ref":6,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["improved uncanny dodge","trap sense +4"],"dr":"4/-","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40,"special":"55 ft. without armor"}],"melee":"+1 thundering earth breaker +19 (2d6+7/19- 20/x3), +1 klar +19 (1d6+4), bite +14 (1d4+3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"greater rage","details":"31 rounds/day"},{"type":"rage powers","details":"animal fury, clear mind, increase damage reduction +1, rolling dodge +3, scent, swift foot +5 ft."}],"strength":22,"dexterity":15,"constitution":22,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":10,"charisma":12,"baseatk":13,"cmb":19,"cmd":31,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Critical (earth breaker)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Shield Focus"},{"feat":"Thunder and Fang"},{"feat":"Two-weapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (earth breaker)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (klar)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":16,"special":"+4 to jump"},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":17},{"skill":"Ride","value":16},{"skill":"Survival","value":16}],"languages":["Common","Shoanti"],"sq":["fast movement"],"special_abilities":[{"type":"Thunder and Fang","details":"This feat (from page 10 of Pathfinder Player Companion: Varisia, Birthplace of Legends) allows Krojun to wield his earth breaker and klar simultaneously in combat, as if he were fighting with a double weapon. When he uses an earth breaker in one hand and a klar in his off hand, Krojun retains the shield bonus his klar grants even when he uses it to attack, and treats his earth breaker as a one-handed weapon and his klar as a light weapon for the purpose of determining his two-weapon fighting penalty."}],"gear":"+2 hide armor, +1 klar, +1 thundering earth breaker, amulet of natural armor +1, boots of striding and springing, Shoanti war paint (3, orange), 3 garnets worth 50 gp each, potion of cure serious wounds (2), potion of shield of faith +2 (4)","before_combat":"If Krojun knows he is about to face great opposition, he applies his Shoanti war paint and drinks a potion of shield of faith +2.","during_combat":"Krojun charges fearlessly into battle, preferring to fight toe-to-toe against foes to make full use of his Thunder and Fang fighting style. Krojun is fond of screaming his own name whenever he lands a critical hit against a foe.","morale":"Headstrong, Krojun has courage to spare. He isn't a fool, however, and withdraws if vastly outnumbered or overmatched, or upon being reduced to 20 hit points or fewer. Only when raging does he fight to the death.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4"},{"name":"Skoan-Quah Boneslayer","cr":4,"xp":1200,"race":"human","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"oracle","level":3},{"class":"ranger","level":2}],"alignment":"CN","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":2,"ac":17,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+4 armor, +2 Dex, +1 dodge","hp":46,"hd":"3d8+2d10+18","hd_value":5,"fort":6,"ref":6,"will":3,"save_mods":"+2 insight bonus vs. diseases, mind-affecting, poison","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"mwk earth breaker +7 (2d6+3/x3)","ranged":"mwk composite longbow +7 (1d8+2/x3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"combat style (two-handed weapon)"},{"type":"favored enemy","details":"undead +2"}],"spellsknown_caster":"oracle","spellsknown_caster_level":3,"spellsknown_concentration":5,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"cause fear"},{"spell":"cure light wounds"},{"spell":"detect undead"},{"spell":"hide from undead"},{"spell":"sanctuary"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"create water"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"purify food and drink"}]}],"mystery":"bones","strength":14,"dexterity":14,"constitution":14,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":10,"charisma":15,"baseatk":4,"cmb":6,"cmd":19,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Totem Spirit (Skoan-Quah)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Heal","value":10},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":6},{"skill":"Perception","value":8},{"skill":"Stealth","value":8},{"skill":"Survival","value":8}],"languages":["Common","Shoanti"],"sq":["oracle's curse (haunted)","revelations (near death, voice of the grave)","track +1","wild empathy +4"],"gear":"mwk hide armor, mwk composite longbow (+2 Str), mwk earth breaker, Shoanti war paint (white), 95 gp, potion of cure light wounds (3), potion of lesser restoration","during_combat":"The boneslayers prefer to fire their bows from covered positions, but if one of them is attacked in melee, the others quickly come to her aid. Once the PCs earn at least 10 Respect Points, the boneslayers are willing to alter their tactics to whatever the PCs want.","morale":"The boneslayers fight to the death.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4, Pathfinder RPG Advanced Player's Guide 42"},{"name":"Sklar-Quah Thundercaller","cr":7,"xp":3200,"race":"human","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"skald","level":8}],"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":7,"ac":20,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+5 armor, +3 deflection, +3 Dex, -1 rage","hp":87,"hd":"8d8+48","hd_value":8,"fort":11,"ref":5,"will":10,"save_mods":"+4 vs. bardic performance, language-dependent, and sonic","defensive_abilities":["improved uncanny dodge"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":25}],"melee":"+1 totem spear +11 (1d10+7/x3)","ranged":"totem spear +9 (1d10+6/x3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"rage powers","details":"guarded stance +2, swift foot +5 ft."},{"type":"raging song 20 rounds/day","details":"move action; inspired rage, song of marching, song of strength"},{"type":"spell kenning","details":"1/day"}],"spellsknown_caster":"skald","spellsknown_caster_level":8,"spellsknown_concentration":11,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":3,"spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"cure serious wounds"},{"spell":"dispel magic"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"gallant inspiration"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"},{"spell":"shatter"},{"spell":"sound burst"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"cure light wounds"},{"spell":"expeditious retreat"},{"spell":"feather fall"},{"spell":"lesser confusion"},{"spell":"saving finale"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"summon instrument"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":16,"constitution":20,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":8,"charisma":16,"baseatk":6,"cmb":10,"cmd":25,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Exotic Weapon Proficiency (totem spear)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Scribe Scroll"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":10},{"skill":"Perform (percussion instruments)","value":14},{"skill":"Perform (wind instruments)","value":14},{"skill":"Ride","value":8},{"skill":"Survival","value":7}],"languages":["Common"],"sq":["bardic knowledge +4","lore master 1/day","rage powers","versatile performance (percussion, wind)"],"special_abilities":[{"type":"Totem Spear","details":"A totem spear is a 6-pound, exotic two-handed melee weapon that deals piercing or slashing damage. A character proficient with a totem spear can use the holes in the spear's shovel-like head to create eerie whistling music with Perform (wind instruments). Totem spears are detailed on page 14 of Pathfinder Player's Companion: Varisia, Birthplace of Legends (note that the rules presented in this stat block correct the totem spear's damage type to piercing and slashing, rather than piercing and bludgeoning)."}],"gear":"+1 hide armor, +1 totem spear, totem spears (3), Shoanti war paint (silver, 2), 35 gp, potion of cure moderate wounds (2), wand of cat's grace (15 charges), wand of cure light wounds (30 charges)","before_combat":"A thundercaller puts on his war paint and uses his wand of cat's grace once a fight seems likely.","during_combat":"One thundercaller activates his inspiring rage while the others engage in melee. The first thundercaller supports the melee fighters with healing magic or casts ranged spells; when a thundercaller in melee is reduced to 30 or fewer hit points, that skald falls back and swaps position and roles with the previous thundercaller.","morale":"As long as Krojun lives, the thundercallers fight to the death. If Krojun dies or is otherwise incapacitated, the thundercallers abandon the acropolis immediately-in this case, they speak ill of the PCs.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4, Pathfinder RPG Advanced Class Guide 49"},{"name":"Lyrune-Quah Moon Maiden","cr":6,"xp":2400,"race":"human","gender":"Female","age_category":"Adult","classes":[{"class":"barbarian","level":1},{"class":"ranger","level":6}],"alignment":"CG","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":1,"ac":15,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+5 armor, +1 Dex, +1 dodge, -2 rage","hp":92,"hd":"6d10+1d12+48","hd_value":7,"fort":13,"ref":6,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"+1 starknife +11 (1d6+5/x3), +1 starknife +11 (1d6+3/x3)","ranged":"starknife +9 (1d6+5/x3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"combat style","details":"two-weapon combat"},{"type":"favored enemy","details":"giants +4, magical beasts +2"},{"type":"rage","details":"8 rounds/day"}],"spellsprepared_caster":"ranger","spellsprepared_caster_level":3,"spellsprepared_concentration":4,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":2,"spells":[{"spell":"lead blades"},{"spell":"longstrider"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":13,"constitution":22,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":7,"cmb":11,"cmd":21,"feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Extra Rage"},{"feat":"Improved Two-Weapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Quick Draw"},{"feat":"Totem Spirit (Lyrune-Quah)"},{"feat":"Two-Weapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (starknife)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":9},{"skill":"Climb","value":12},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":8},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9},{"skill":"Survival","value":11}],"languages":["Common","Shoanti"],"sq":["fast movement","favored terrain (desert +2)","hunter's bond (companions)","track +3","wild empathy +6"],"gear":"+1 hide armor, +1 starknives (2), starknives (6)","before_combat":"The moon maidens each cast lead blades and longstrider before entering combat.","during_combat":"The moon maidens rage when combat begins, hurling their nonmagical starknives at their enemies for the first few rounds. Once they're down to only their magical starknives, they rush in to engage foes in melee. If they're fighting with allies, one moon maiden activates her hunter's bond to share her bonuses, with the others activating their bonds in turn when the previous one wears off.","morale":"A moon maiden fights until brought to fewer than 10 hit points, at which point she flees to recover and plan her second assault on the enemy. A moon maiden who is raging doesn't flee, but fights to the death.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4"},{"name":"Akram","cr":7,"xp":3200,"race":"human","gender":"Male","age_category":"Old","classes":[{"class":"cleric of Desna","level":8}],"alignment":"CG","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","sub_types":["human"],"init":-1,"senses":["discern lies"],"ac":12,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":12,"ac_mods":"+3 armor, -1 Dex","hp":47,"hd":"8d8+8","hd_value":8,"fort":7,"ref":2,"will":14,"immunities":["charm","compulsion"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"+1 returning starknife +5 (1d4-1/x3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"channel positive energy","details":"6/day, DC 17, 4d6"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dimensional hop","details":"80 feet/day"}]},{"frequency":"8/day","spells":[{"spell":"bit of luck"}]}],"spellsprepared_caster":"cleric","spellsprepared_caster_level":8,"spellsprepared_concentration":13,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"dimension door","type":"domain"},{"spell":"divination"},{"spell":"sending"},{"spell":"tongues"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"fly","type":"domain"},{"spell":"magic vestment"},{"spell":"prayer"},{"spell":"remove disease"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"aid","type":"domain"},{"spell":"calm emotions"},{"spell":"enthrall"},{"spell":"spiritual weapon"},{"spell":"zone of truth"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"command"},{"spell":"endure elements"},{"spell":"longstrider","type":"domain"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"protection from evil"},{"spell":"sanctuary"},{"spell":"shield of faith"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"create water"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"purify food and drink"}]}],"spelldomains":"Luck, Travel","strength":6,"dexterity":9,"constitution":10,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":20,"charisma":16,"baseatk":6,"cmb":4,"cmd":13,"feats":[{"feat":"Craft Magic Arms and Armor"},{"feat":"Craft Wand"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Selective Channeling"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Sense Motive)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":12},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":6},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":19},{"skill":"Survival","value":13}],"languages":["Common","Dwarven","Elven","Giant","Shoanti"],"sq":["agile feet (8/day)","good fortune (1/day)"],"special_abilities":[{"type":"Truthspeaker","kind":"Su","details":"Akram has undertaken a lifelong quest of fasting, meditation, exploration, and prayer to achieve the status of truthspeaker. This has granted him immunity to all charm and compulsion effects. Furthermore, he is constantly under the effects of discern lies (CL 7th)."}],"gear":"padded armor, +1 returning starknife, cloak of resistance +1, wand of cure moderate wounds (32 charges), wand of lesser restoration (20 charges)","before_combat":"Akram casts magic vestment on his robes every day after breakfast.","during_combat":"Akram prefers to save his spells for healing or support. He generally casts prayer on the first round of battle, followed by spiritual weapon and then sanctuary, so he can move about the fringe of combat to heal allies in relative safety.","morale":"Akram has little interest in combat, and if confronted while alone or if reduced to fewer than 10 hit points, he casts dimension door to escape immediate danger and then fly to flee to a place of safety.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4"},{"name":"Cindermaw","cr":14,"xp":38400,"race":"purple worm","age_category":"Adult","alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"magical beast","sub_types":["fire"],"templates_applied":"advanced, fire infused","init":1,"senses":["darkvision 60 ft.","low-light vision","tremorsense 60 ft."],"ac":31,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":30,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +24 natural, -4 size","hp":216,"hd":"16d10+128","hd_value":16,"hp_mods":"fire healing 1","fort":18,"ref":11,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["elemental body"],"immunities":["fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"burrow","speed":20},{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"swim","speed":10}],"melee":"bite +26 (4d8+13/19-20 plus 1d6 fire and grab), sting +26 (2d8+13 plus 1d6 fire)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fire breath"},{"type":"heat","details":"1d6 fire"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"4d8+18, AC 22, 21 hp"}],"strength":37,"dexterity":12,"constitution":27,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":8,"charisma":14,"baseatk":16,"cmb":33,"cmb_special":"+35 bull rush, +37 grapple","cmd":44,"cmd_special":"46 vs. bull rush, can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (sting)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Swim","value":21}],"special_abilities":[{"type":"Bonus Feat","details":"Rather than receive Quick Draw as a bonus feat from the element-infused creature template, Cindermaw gained Iron Will as a bonus feat."},{"type":"Elemental Body","kind":"Ex","details":"Each time Cindermaw is exposed to a bleed, precision damage, poison, paralysis, seep, or stunning effect, it has a 25% chance to avoid that effect."},{"type":"Fire Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Cindermaw can breathe out a 30-foot cone of fire once every 1d4 rounds, dealing 8d6 points of fire damage to all in the area of effect. A successful DC 26 Reflex saving throw halves this damage. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Fire Healing","kind":"Ex","details":"Cindermaw regains 1 hit point for each full round it remains in contact with a fire at least one size category smaller than itself. When struck by a magical fire effect, Cindermaw regains 1 hit point for every 10 points of damage that the fire effect would otherwise deal."},{"type":"Firewalk","kind":"Su","details":"Cindermaw can climb an object on fire as though it had a climb speed of 30 feet. It can also fly at this speed with perfect maneuverability as long as it remains in contact with fire, and can walk on flames at its highest speed as per air walk."},{"type":"Heat","kind":"Su","details":"Each of Cindermaw's attacks deals an extra 1d6 points of fire damage."}],"during_combat":"When Cindermaw tires of toying with the PCs, it burrows up directly in their midst. Unfortunately, Cindermaw has recently fed. On the first round of combat, it breathes fire on the most densely packed group of PCs. It then attacks with its bite and sting on the second round of combat. It doesn't try to swallow foes whole immediately-instead, it bites and moves on. Once the PCs deal more than 100 points of damage to the worm (or once it has breathed fire twice), it abandons this tactic and begins attempting to swallow victims. Alternatively, a character can tempt the worm into swallowing her by attempting a Bluff check to appear particularly appetizing and worth the risk of a stomach ache; she takes a -10 penalty on the check due to the bluff's far-fetched believability. Cindermaw can oppose this check with a Sense Motive check.","morale":"Cindermaw retreats if it takes more than 80 points of damage in all from cold attacks, or as soon as it is reduced to fewer than 50 hit points.","source":"Curse Of The Crimson Throne Chapter 4, Advanced Bestiary 139, Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 230"}];
